WEB SOURCE (the specification) — components/feedback/AchievementUnlockListener.tsx (+ the toast + hooks it binds)
  AchievementUnlockListener.tsx — mounts at the app root; drains the realtime `achievement_unlocked` SSE queue
    via useAchievementUnlocks(), reads useAchievementCelebrationPrefs(), plays an optional procedural chime, and
    renders the celebration toast stack:
      • useAchievementUnlocks(): `recent` newest-first, de-duped by achievement.id, bounded MAX_RECENT=25;
        `dismiss(id)` filters one out.
      • useAchievementCelebrationPrefs(): { showToasts (default on), playSound (default off), … }.
      • chime: useEffect([recent.length, prefs.playSound]) — if playSound && recent.length>0, synthesize a
        two-note WebAudio "ding" (E5 659.25 → B5 987.77, triangle, peak 0.18, 0.02s attack, 0.45s decay, 0.5s/note,
        0.12s stagger); wrapped in try/catch (silent no-op if WebAudio is unavailable). Runs BEFORE the
        `!showToasts` early return, so the chime is independent of the visible-toast opt-out.
      • `if (!prefs.showToasts) return null` — suppress visible toasts but keep draining + chiming.
      • else <AchievementUnlockedToastStack events={recent} onDismiss={dismiss} />.
  AchievementUnlockedToast.tsx — per event: [AchievementBadge][eyebrow "Achievement Unlocked" + name + description
    + "View →"][× dismiss]; auto-dismiss durationMs=6000; View → navigate('/lifetime?achievement=' +
    encodeURIComponent(id)); role="status" aria-live="polite"; confetti + spring honour reduced-motion.

