PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  AchievementUnlockedToast              -> AchievementUnlockListenerToastRow (own rich row; the shared atom
                                           TSAchievementUnlockedToast is title-only and cannot carry description /
                                           View / dismiss / badge, so — like AiLimitBanner built its own card —
                                           the row is composed from TSButton + tokens + TSFadeIn).
  AchievementUnlockedToastStack         -> AchievementUnlockListenerToastStack (VStack, newest-first).
  useAchievementUnlocks / …Prefs        -> P1/S8 AchievementUnlockListenerSource -> …Model (no view HTTP).
  WebAudio chime                        -> AchievementUnlockListenerSystemChime (AVFoundation procedural synth);
                                           tone parameters live in the pure …ChimeSpec, asserted vs the web values.
  navigate('/lifetime?achievement=…')   -> AchievementUnlockListenerRoute.lifetime (encodeURIComponent parity).
  yellow-500/40 chrome, text-yellow-300 -> brand amber statusWarning token at the web fill/border opacities
                                           (ADR-006 semantic, light+dark safe).
  role=status / aria-live=polite        -> combined a11y label on the copy block + AccessibilityNotification
                                           .Announcement on a new head toast; View + dismiss carry their own labels.
  i18n                                  -> every string via AchievementUnlockListenerStrings (P1/S10); verbatim web
                                           fallbacks (achievements.toastEyebrow / .view / .dismiss) + native chrome.
  telemetry                             -> view.opened surface="AchievementUnlockListener" once on appear (P1/S11).
  Reduce Motion                         -> TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton shimmer honour accessibilityReduceMotion.

  Parity decision (logged, no silent drift): the web chime effect keys on `recent.length` and plays whenever
  length>0, so it re-fires on a dismiss-driven length change; the documented source intent is to chime once per NEW
  unlock (dismiss removes acknowledged entries). The native model reproduces the INTENT — it chimes on a queue
  GROWTH (a new unlock) while playSound is on, never on a dismiss-driven decrease — and a unit test pins this.

STATES (every web render branch + P4 leaf state reproduced — never a hidden/blank surface)
  loading              : skeleton toast chrome (SSE feed resolving).
  empty(noUnlocks)     : friendly "No new achievements" (web empty `recent` steady state).
  empty(celebrationsOff): friendly "Celebrations are off" (web `if (!prefs.showToasts) return null`; the queue still
                          drains + the chime still plays — both verified).
  unavailable          : retry tile (web QueryError peer; the SSE-failure branch — a P4 leaf state).
  ready                : the celebration toast stack (one row per queued unlock).
  stale                : freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the rising edge.
  offline              : freshness chip over the cached toasts (no auto-refresh while offline).
  Each state has a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test.

